  <prompt>Extend RuleSetService and RuleSetEndpoints for the four scope levels (notes/rule-set-scope-design.md sections 4.1-4.4): validate scope and core record on create, assign and publish; require Read and AppendTo on the core record; lock a Published set's scope (409 ruleset.scope_locked); write the business-unit list; route the rule set, policy and version creates through IRecordOwnershipResolver with the core record as parent; move the census from Waived to Routed with the narrower guard and its ontology twin; add sprk_ruleset to the secure lineage with three-hop tests; send uac-r2 the D-120 extension.</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Expert in ASP.NET Core Minimal APIs, the Finance authorization filter, IRecordOwnershipResolver and the uac-r2 secure-family model.</role>

  <goal>A record-scoped rule set can be created, assigned and published only with a valid scope and core record and with the caller's Read + AppendTo on it; its set, policies and versions are owned through the resolver (Secure team for a Secure record); the census lists the three creates as Routed; the guards and the lineage tests pass with their must-fire controls; uac-r2 has the D-120 extension.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Design note sections 4.1-4.5, 5.1, 5.3, 12 (ontology-r1 conditions 1-2). Decisions: D-136 / ontology D-171; D-137 / ontology D-172 (Q9 lock, Q10 cleanup, no Restrict). Current code: RuleSetScope enum (RuleSetService.cs:21); create :387-399 and :405; AddDraftsAsync :871; CreateDraftRuleAsync :1060-1100; EditAsync new version :1277; publish scope check :1541-1555; AssignAsync :1910-1947 (Published re-scope allowed today, Retired refused :1919-1922); Summarize :2242; OwnerContext :2389-2393. Endpoints: RuleSetEndpoints.cs TryParseScope :227-231, :478; AssignCallers reason :770-772. Census: tests/Spaarke.ArchTests/RecordOwnerAssignmentCensusTests.cs ChildTables :47-61, RuleSetServicePolicyWaiver :127-139, entries :265-266, UnscannedWriters :306.</background>
