  <constraints>
    <constraint source="design note 4.1">Create, assign and publish each apply the 4.1 matrix and return 400 ruleset.invalid (publish: ruleset.publish_invalid) with the listed field errors. Record and FirmRecord need exactly one existing core lookup; ClientDefault and Firm take none. matterId, projectId and workAssignmentId are query parameters on create and on PUT /{id}/assignment (078 doctrine, RateCardImportEndpoints.cs:20-22, :166-187). The BU ids go in RuleSetAssignmentBody (AllBusinessUnits, BusinessUnitIds); each must exist, and the Secure Record business unit (SecureRecordOwnerTeam.BusinessUnitNameConfigKey, "SecureRecord:BusinessUnitName") is refused with field businessUnits (it never matches a list, design note 5.2).</constraint>
    <constraint source="design note 4.1, root CLAUDE.md section 6">Every route that names a core record checks, as the caller, a new OperationAccessPolicy key ebilling.ruleset.scope = Read | AppendTo, through the same FinanceAuthorizationCheck Record path RateCardImportEndpoints.cs:120-133 uses (copy it; do not reuse finance.submit_invoice or finance.read). Refusal is 403 from the filter before the service runs.</constraint>
    <constraint source="D-137 / ontology D-172 Q9">AssignAsync on a Published set that changes scope, firm, core record or BU list returns 409 ruleset.scope_locked ("Retire this rule set and create a new one for the new scope."), Firm sets included. A Draft change is allowed and re-owns the set, its policies and versions through IRecordOwnershipResolver.ReparentAsync (listed in UnscannedWriters).</constraint>
    <constraint source="design note 4.2">The S3 flag and the N:N associate / disassociate are written as the app identity in the same call; associates are idempotent; a partial failure is 500 ruleset.write_failed. Publish re-reads the list and refuses No with an empty list. RuleSetSummary gains AllBusinessUnits, BusinessUnitIds and coreRecord {type, id, name} (additive members).</constraint>
    <constraint source="D-171 Q3, design note 4.4">Record and FirmRecord sets: ResolveOwnerAsync(RecordOwnershipContext.ForParents([core record], caller) with { RequestedBy = caller }) at create (:405), AddDraftsAsync (:871) and EditAsync (:1277), as RateCardImportService.cs:200-211 does. ClientDefault and Firm: unchanged (no parents). A refusal writes nothing (409 OwnerRefused).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ontology-r1 Q14 condition 1 (note section 12)">In the same change: census sprk_policy / sprk_policyversion Waived → Routed, new entry ("RuleSetService.cs", "sprk_ruleset", 1, Routed), RuleSetServicePolicyWaiver deleted, sprk_ruleset in ChildTables. RuleSetServiceNoMatterScopeGuardTests replaced by the narrower guard "no sprk_matter written on a PolicyEntity or VersionEntity row". Twin guard: OntologyAdminAuthoringService never writes sprk_ruleset. Both guards have a must-fire and a must-not-fire control and a seeding proof. RuleSetServiceOwnerTests.NoWrittenPolicyOrVersionRowCarriesAMatter_OnCreateOrUpdate stays unchanged. ontology-r1 reviews both guards.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ontology-r1 Q14 condition 2">SecureChildLineage: new sprk_ruleset entry (sprk_matter → Matter, sprk_project → Project, sprk_workassignment → WorkAssignment) and ("sprk_ruleset", "sprk_ruleset") on sprk_policy; sprk_ruleset in OwnershipParentEntities. SecureFamilyConsistencyTests and a SecureChildReconciler test cover version → policy → ruleset → core end to end, on secure and on unsecure. CitationLookups unchanged.</constraint>
    <constraint source="D-137 / ontology D-172 Q10">No delete-Restrict and no delete handling in this task. Send uac-r2 the D-120 extension as a notice (comment on #2129 and a message to the uac-r2 session): a record's own Record / FirmRecord rule set (with policies and versions) and its own rate card are deleted with the record, or retired if something that survives the delete cites one of their versions. The delete step is uac-r2's code.</constraint>
    <constraint source=".claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md">BFF hygiene: placement (existing RuleSetService and endpoints), publish-size delta against a fresh master build, no new package, no new HIGH CVE.</constraint>
  </constraints>

