    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0">git merge-base --is-ancestor 3c83d48cf HEAD; read notes/080-ruleset-scope-schema.md for the live names and values.</step>
    <step order="1">RuleSetScope gains Record = 100000002 and FirmRecord = 100000003; Summarize and TryParseScope name them.</step>
    <step order="2">Validation matrix (4.1) on create, assign, publish; query-parameter inputs; BU body members; RuleSetSummary members.</step>
    <step order="3">OperationAccessPolicy key and the endpoint checks; contract test for 403 without AppendTo.</step>
    <step order="4">Q9 lock in AssignAsync; Draft re-scope re-owns through ReparentAsync.</step>
    <step order="5">Owner routing at the three create sites; RuleSetServiceOwnerTests additions.</step>
    <step order="6">Census, narrower guard, twin guard (with seeding proofs); SecureChildLineage, OwnershipParentEntities, lineage and three-hop tests.</step>
    <step order="7">Only after uac-r2 answers Q11: S5 role row in config/secure-record-owner-role.json and the List / Get filter by the caller's Read on the core record (design note 5.3), with tests. If Q11 is unanswered, leave both out and record them as the open part.</step>
    <step order="8">D-120 extension notice to uac-r2; record it.</step>
    <step order="9">dotnet build; dotnet test (unit, ArchTests, contract); publish-size delta; /conflict-check.</step>
    <step order="10">Update TASK-INDEX.md: this task's status cell to "✅ [done]" (or keep 🟡 with the Q11 part named if step 7 is open).</step>
    <step order="11">Record deviations in projects/ebilling-r1/notes/081-ruleset-scope-service.md.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>Q11 open: if uac-r2 has not answered Q11 (secure family membership, Read depth on sprk_ruleset, admin visibility), do NOT edit config/secure-record-owner-role.json and do NOT add the List / Get filter; finish the rest and report the open part.</trigger>
    <trigger>If the Basic User Read depth on sprk_ruleset is Organization (S5 check), STOP and raise 🔔 Human Input Required: a Secure-team owner would hide nothing, and changing a role is uac-r2's and the owner's call.</trigger>
    <trigger>If ontology-r1 or uac-r2 rejects the guard, twin guard or lineage change in review, STOP; do not weaken a guard to make it pass.</trigger>
    <trigger>If routing through the resolver needs a resolver change in RecordOwnershipResolver.cs beyond adding sprk_ruleset to OwnershipParentEntities, STOP and ask uac-r2.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>RuleSetService, RuleSetEndpoints and the 076 validation exist and are extended; OperationAccessPolicy has finance.read (Read) and finance.submit_invoice (Read | AppendTo) at :174 and :201; the census and SecureChildLineage already list sprk_policy.</existing>
    <extension>All behaviour extends existing files. One new operation key, because neither existing key names this act (a deny would read "submit invoice", the precedent noted at OperationAccessPolicy.cs:251-253). One new guard test file and one new reconciler test file hold the two new controls.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>A matter-scoped rule set cannot be created; if it were, a caller without AppendTo could attach terms to any record, and a Secure matter's set, policies and versions would sit in the ordinary business unit (visible across the wall).</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <tools>
    <tool name="dotnet">build, test</tool>
    <tool name="conflict-check">before the PR</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">RuleSetService.cs, RuleSetEndpoints.cs, OperationAccessPolicy.cs, SecureChildLineage.cs, RecordOwnershipResolver.cs, config/secure-record-owner-role.json (if Q11 answered)</output>
    <output type="test">the test files listed in relevant-files</output>
    <output type="docs">projects/ebilling-r1/notes/081-ruleset-scope-service.md</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Each row of the 4.1 matrix has one passing test for its field error on create, assign and publish; a valid Record and FirmRecord set is created and published.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A caller without AppendTo on the named core record gets 403 from the filter and nothing is written; a caller with Read + AppendTo passes (contract test).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Changing scope, firm, core record or BU list of a Published set (Firm included) returns 409 ruleset.scope_locked and writes nothing; the same change on a Draft succeeds and re-owns the set, its policies and versions.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Publish with AllBusinessUnits No and an empty list returns ruleset.publish_invalid with field businessUnits; a list with an unknown business unit, or with the Secure Record business unit, is refused.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A record-scoped create passes exactly [core record] as parents; a Secure matter yields the Secure team as owner of the set, policy and version; a client-default create passes none.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The census lists sprk_policy and sprk_policyversion as Routed and the new sprk_ruleset entry; RuleSetServicePolicyWaiver is gone; EveryRoutedEntryRoutesThroughTheResolver passes.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The narrower guard fails on a planted policy["sprk_matter"] write and passes on ruleSet["sprk_matter"]; the twin guard fails on a planted sprk_ruleset write in OntologyAdminAuthoringService; each has a recorded seeding proof.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">SecureFamilyConsistencyTests and the SecureChildReconciler test cover version → policy → ruleset → core on secure and on unsecure; SecureChildLineageTests include sprk_ruleset.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The D-120 extension notice to uac-r2 is recorded in the notes. No delete-Restrict and no delete code is added.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">If Q11 is answered: the S5 role row exists and List / Get leave out a record-scoped set whose core record the caller cannot Read. If not: neither is added, and the notes name the open part.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Publish-size delta recorded; no new package; no new HIGH CVE; /conflict-check run.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Cover the stated contract plus the edge cases named above. Anything beyond that needs a one-line justification in task notes.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Two adversarial-review passes (auth, tenant-isolation). The applicability predicate (RuleSetApplicability) is 082's, not this task's. The Rule Review UI is 084's.</notes>

